  "rationale": "No evidence-supported optimization has verified prerequisites for this workflow. The dependency-cache pattern (P-LIT-GHA-CACHE) is contraindicated because every job already uses `setup-node` with `cache: npm`, so an equivalent cache exists. The fail-fast/matrix-cancellation pattern (P-LIT-FAIL-FAST) does not apply because the workflow has no matrix strategy. A custom job timeout (P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT, experiment:batch-interactive-three--fb8b16eb65a11508) requires representative successful-duration history, but the available CI history is run-level only, marked not_a_measured_baseline/historical_context_only, and lacks per-job durations; imposing an arbitrary timeout (e.g., 5 minutes) on the `test` (`nx affected:test --ci --code-coverage`) and `build` (`nx affected:build`) jobs risks terminating valid slow runs and weakening the intended build/test coverage. No other pattern's preconditions are met, so the workflow is left unchanged to preserve coverage and avoid unsafe changes.",
